---
// In-page closure callout. The site-wide banner is the persistent signal; this
// is for pages whose body copy describes a product that is no longer for sale.
---
<div class="closed-notice">
  <slot>
    <strong>Liv is shutting down.</strong>
    The platform is closed to new signups and shuts down on <strong>26 September 2026</strong>;
    all user data is permanently deleted on 26 October 2026.
    <a href="/shutdown">read the shutdown notice &rarr;</a>
  </slot>
</div>

<style>
  .closed-notice {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 16px);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .closed-notice :global(strong) { color: var(--text); }
  .closed-notice :global(a) { color: var(--amber, #fbbf24); }
</style>
